* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary

# These fixtures' whole reason to exist is a literal CRLF (or bare CR)
# checkout — they prove checkNoMarkers/checkNoMarkersFlat's G2 check fires
# on real bytes. The blanket `eol=lf` above would silently normalize them
# away on the next checkin, so each root is exempted and stored/checked out
# byte-for-byte instead.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: within one .gitattributes file, the LAST matching
# line wins per attribute, not the most specific pattern. These `-text`
# lines must stay BELOW the blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above — move
# one above it and the blanket rule becomes the last match again, silently
# reinstating `eol=lf` and breaking the fixture it was written to protect.
# Any future rule added above this comment block re-triggers the same trap.
test/fixtures/crlf-skills/** -text
test/fixtures/crlf-roles/** -text
